57585787773], ["-*", -3.596698522567749]]}], "text": "Here's a summary of the session notes in 8 bullet points:\n\n- **Scope & context:** A two-part rebuild series of the `llama.cpp-sycl-f16-git` AUR package (Raudbjorn fork) on host `vinbonesjr` (Ryzen 7900X3D + Intel Arc A770 16GB), spanning 2026-09-26 to 2026-10-01 across two Claude contexts (Opus 5.5 then Sonnet 5.5), covering commits b10146 \u2192 b12321.\n\n- **Major technical work:** The session addressed a PKGBUILD rework, an LLAMA_SUBPROCESS ABI compatibility trap (commit d37dd50bb), SYCL graph optimizations, a oneDNN A/B comparison, a oneAPI 2026.0 \u2192 2026.1 upgrade (DLE swap), PR #63, and a DG2 XMX-gather IGC crash patch (commit 4e7400c3a).\n\n- **Driver/kernel transition:** The Intel Arc A770 switched from the i915 driver (kernel 7.3.0-rc1) to the **xe** driver (kernel 7.3.0-rc5) between the two contexts\u2014handled by other sessions\u2014with the AMD iGPU continuing to drive the monitors.\n\n- **Benchmarking:** Extensive performance analysis including 256-GRF kernel builds, perplexity A/B testing, llama-bench attempts, and a \"12-vs-18 tokens/second decode investigation,\" with data stored in `~/research-llama.cpp/sycl-oneapi-benchmarks-2026-"}